    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



a) Write out the terms for each value of <m>i</m> from 3 to 5,
then add the terms.
<me>\begin{array}{rcl}
    i = 3 \amp \to\amp  a_{3} = (3)^2 = 9\\
    i = 4 \amp \to\amp  a_{4} = (4)^2 = 16\\
    i = 5 \amp \to\amp  a_{5} = (5)^2 = 25\\
  \end{array}</me>
The sum is: <m>\displaystyle\sum_{i=3}^{5} i^2  = 50</m> 




b) Write out the terms for each value of <m>i</m> from -3 to 2,
then add the terms.
<me>\begin{array}{rcl}
    i = -3 \amp \to\amp  a_{-3} = 5(-3)  - 7 = -22\\
    i = -2 \amp \to\amp  a_{-2} = 5(-2)  - 7 = -17\\
    i = -1 \amp \to\amp  a_{-1} = 5(-1)  - 7 = -12\\
    i = 0 \amp \to\amp  a_{0} = 5(0)  - 7 = -7\\
    i = 1 \amp \to\amp  a_{1} = 5(1)  - 7 = -2\\
    i = 2 \amp \to\amp  a_{2} = 5(2)  - 7 = 3\\
  \end{array}</me>
The sum is: <m>\displaystyle\sum_{i=-3}^{2} (5 i  - 7)  = -57</m> 


</solution>
